    "President Prabowo Subianto is scheduled to deliver two vice presidential candidate names to the MPR on November 25, 2026.",
    "The MPR Ad Hoc Committee has confirmed the receipt of these names is anticipated for the upcoming week.",
    "Political leaders, including Puan Maharani, have expressed respect for the President's selection process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is currently moving toward the selection of a new vice president following vacancy developments. Benny K. Harman, chairman of the MPR Ad Hoc Committee, stated that President Prabowo Subianto is expected to personally present two candidate names to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) on November 25, 2026. This process follows initial discussions regarding the transition and potential candidates, including speculation regarding political figures like Sufmi Dasco Ahmad. Defense Minister Sjafrie Sjamsoeddin clarified that no official discussions regarding vice presidential candidates occurred during recent meetings with DPR leadership. Political parties, such as the PDI-P, have indicated they will not submit their own candidate names, choosing instead to respect the prerogative of the President to make the final appointment. The MPR has begun formal proceedings to address the vice presidential vacancy, aiming for a resolution by the specified date.",
